At 08:38 AM 3/26/04 +0000, kainhart wrote:
>I've tried suggesting this a few times in different places in the
>lojban community but I don't seem to get any responses. I'm very much
>interested in learning lojban. I'm a native speaker of American
>English and I am studying Japanese now. I have made a lot of friends
>interested in Lojban who have limited abilities in english. I wish is
>for more resources about lojban in Japanese. If I learn lojban in the
>future I will be willing to help this effort but something if there
>was something out there in advanced it would help to motivate me and
>probably many other Japanese speaking people to learn this
>interesting langauge. So please if there are any Lojban resources in
>Japanese that already exist please post them here, or if somebody is
>interested in helping out with such a project please also post your
>thoughts.

I don't know of any Japanese resources for Lojban.  There is one native 
English Lojbanist living in Japan, Dave Young, who might be interested in 
helping you, but otherwise there is no one I know who is competent enough 
in Japanese to even work on such a thing.  There have been a few Japanese 
over the years showing some interest in Lojban, but I don't know any who 
have stuck with it.

